				<h1 id="versionHeadLine" class="headline">

Elections		</h1>
	
		<div id="cc4ab169fa-d684-411c-8edd-6871b31e5d38" data-containerid="4ab169fa-d684-411c-8edd-6871b31e5d38" class="pageContent cpGrid cpGrid24"  >
			

		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="ae02520c-64a8-45d8-8ed2-c2792364860a">				
	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last idab09a5e7-3071-49fc-80fb-a3330b04cb9a" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="ab09a5e7-3071-49fc-80fb-a3330b04cb9a">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor9015a1c8-fea4-4802-8904-2a6fd1719999" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h1 class="headline">ELECTION DATES 2026:</h1><p><strong>State Election: November 3, 2026&nbsp;</strong></p><h3 class="subhead2"><strong>STATE ELECTION SAMPLE BALLOTS:</strong></h3><p>Precinct 1,2,3,4a: <a href="/DocumentCenter/View/5926" target="_blank" rel="noopener">State Election Sample Ballot (PDF)</a></p><p>Precinct 4: <a href="/DocumentCenter/View/5927" target="_blank" rel="noopener">State Election Sample Ballot (PDF)</a></p><p><strong><a href="https://ma.omniballot.us/sites/25/vg/app/vig/voter-guide/instructions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ballot Questions (webpage link)</a></strong></p><p><a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/download/research-and-statistics/MA-Info-For-Voters-2026.mp3" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Ballot Questions (Audio link)</strong></a></p><p><strong>Elections are held in the gymnasium at:</strong></p><p>Heritage School<br>34 Oxford Road<br>Charlton, MA 01507</p><p style="margin-left: 40px;"><strong>⇨ State/Federal Elections:</strong> Tuesdays from 7am - 8pm</p><p style="margin-left: 40px;"><strong>⇨Local/Town Elections:&nbsp;</strong>Saturdays from<strong>&nbsp;</strong>8am - 8pm</p><p><strong><a href="https://www.townofcharlton.net/179/Registrars-of-Voters" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Which precinct am I in? (Webpage Link)</a></strong></p><p><strong><a href="https://www.townofcharlton.net/179/Registrars-of-Voters" id="isPasted" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Voter Registration Details and Links (Webpage Link)</a></strong></p><p><a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/WhereDoIVoteMA/WhereDoIVote" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Who are my elected State Officials? (Webpage Link)</strong></a></p><h1 class="headline">VOTE BY MAIL INFORMATION:</h1><p><a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/WhereDoIVoteMA/TrackMyBallot" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>TRACK MY BALLOT (webpage link)</strong></a></p><p><strong><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/5604" target="_blank" rel="noopener">VOTE BY MAIL PAPER APPLICATION (PDF)</a></strong></p><p><strong><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/5901" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ABSENTEE BALLOT APPLICATION (PDF)</a></strong></p><p><a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/MailInRequestWeb/MailInBallot.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>VOTE BY MAIL ELECTRONIC APPLICATION (webpage link)</strong></a></p><p>ALL MAIL IN BALLOTS CAN BE MAILED, HAND DELIVERED TO TOWN CLERK&apos;S OFFICE OR DROPPED IN THE TOWN HALL SECURE DROP BOX LOCATED ON THE BUILDING NEAR ACCESSIBLE PARKING.</p><h3 class="subhead2"><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">ACCESSIBLE VOTE BY MAIL - OMNI BALLOT</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong></h3><p id="isPasted">The Accessible Vote by Mail (AVBM) system allows you to receive, complete, and return your ballot <em>electronically</em> using a secure web portal if you are unable to mark a paper ballot because of a disability. This system is compatible with screen readers.</p><p id="isPasted">The AVBM system is only available to voters who are unable to independently read, write, hold, or physically manipulate or mark ballots. This could be due to:</p><ul type="disc"><li>blindness or&nbsp;vision impairments,</li><li>mobility/dexterity disabilities, or</li><li>other disabilities that make it difficult or impossible to effectively access a paper Vote by Mail ballot, because of inability to independently read, write, hold, or physically manipulate standard print materials. (source: <a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/voting-information/voters-with-disabilities.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Secretary of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts website</a>)</li></ul><p>To request the AVBM <em>electronic</em> ballot, you will need to click on the link below to complete the application process. &nbsp;Please be sure to check the box at the bottom under the <strong>Accommodation</strong> section, stating that you are requesting use of the AVBM system due to a disability. &nbsp;An email address is <strong>REQUIRED</strong> for access.</p><p>The completed ballot can be returned electronically or printed and returned by mail, secure ballot drop box, or in person to your local election office or early voting location.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>NOTE: The deadline to make a request is 5pm on the 5th business day before Election Day.</strong></p><p><a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/MailInRequestWeb/MailInBallot.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Accessible Vote By Mail ELECTRONIC Application (Website Link)</a></p><p><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/5605" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Accessible Vote By Mail PAPER Application (PDF)</a></p><h3 class="subhead2"><strong>MILITARY AND OVERSEAS VOTERS INFO</strong></h3><p><a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/voting-information/military-and-overseas-voters.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Military and Overseas Voter Information from the Secretary of Commonwealth (Website Link)</strong></a></p><p><strong>Military Voters:</strong> <a href="https://www.fvap.gov/military-voter/overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Federal Post Card Application (Website Link)</a></p><p><strong>Overseas Voters:</strong> <a href="https://www.fvap.gov/citizen-voter/overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Federal Post Card Application (Website Link)</a></p>
    </div>

